{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/931736-3rd-ed-ideas-exigent-of-the-beautiful-destruction","id":931736,"title":"[3rd Ed.] Ideas - Exigent of the Beautiful Destruction","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Exigents"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-07-14T18:21:56-07:00","id":931736,"title":"[3rd Ed.] Ideas - Exigent of the Beautiful Destruction","content":"I wanted to do something interesting for my players next session. I have created a Black Market Exaltation that has gone very wrong, and it is going to be unleashed in Nexus by a goddess I created for the campaign: Laitana, the Goddesses of the Silken Death. I loved the concept for kitbashed and repurposed exigent exaltations, and I took the concept and ran with it. <br /> <br /> This exaltation was created for Onaris, the god of a small city of Great Garden, in the Scavenger Lands. This city had a regimented and traditional rules of engagement with its neighbor cities, spanning uncountable generations of warriors and legends. Territories were taken and lost in many skirmishes that were scheduled between the crops. And then the Arczeki Horde came, and their numbers and uncivility took all by surprise. Desperate, Onaris called for an Exigence, and was answered by the Unconquered Sun. Onaris was no more. But the Exaltation never came, and was taken by gods who sold it to someone else, who sold it to someone else, and it was passed along from Yu-Shan underground to Nexus underground, were it was sold to a goddess who was being opposed by at least two solar exalted. <br /> <br /> But, the exaltation had two great flaws. First, as it was being created, the exaltation has been blessed by Amoth City-Smiter, God of Ruins. As such, the exalted by this have a tendency for destruction. Also, the exaltation was kept from its rightful destination, and this has occurred in a huge curse from heaven. <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Excellency - Skill-Based:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> 1m/1d - Allows the Exalt to add up to skill in a dice pool. If the Exalt stunts the beauty of his strike, this allows his to raise his cap to Attribute + Skill.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Permanent Limit Break:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> 8.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Essence Fever:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> The bearer of this Exaltation is overtaken by the will to act and destroy, gaining these two defining intimacies:</span></span><ul><li>Destruction is Beautiful</li> <li>Combat is Beautiful</li> </ul><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Some weeks after the Exaltation, the user may erode these intimacies as he grows accostumed to his new condition. Eroding these intimacies lead to rolling limit break, as a solar would.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Recurring Exaltation: </b>Exigent of the Beautiful Destruction don't have a hightened lifespan, but don't show signs of aging until they die. However, if the bearer dies, the exaltation will seek someone with combat or destruction excellencies in the range of 2 miles, and exalt him right away. If there are none that apply in range, the exaltation dissipates. <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Personal Mores: 7 + 2* essence</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Peripheral Motes: 25 + 4 *essence</span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Anima Markings:</b> A polichromatic sword surrounded by ruins appears in the exalt's forehead when he spends 5 motes peripheral in a turn. <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Sample Charms</span></span></b><br /><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#434343\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Combat</span></span></b><br /><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Beautiful Weapon (Melee or Brawl)</span></span></span></b><br /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost: 8m, 1wp; Mins: Melee 3, Essence 1</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Type: Simple</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Keywords: Amoth</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration: Indefinite</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Pre-reqs: TBD</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Honing her skill and focusing her will, the Exalt imbues her weapon with her essence. This Charm imbues a weapon he has ownership for at least of one week with the stats of an artifact version of itself, as described on page 595. The weapon is beautiful, laquered, and glows like a torch. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Amoth's Blessing:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> The exalted may use an action to destroy an object that has 100 years or more to gain 2 motes. This may be done in a stunt, depending on the fragility of the object in question, and if it's unguarded. This benefit may be gained only once per turn, no matter the quantity of historical objects destroyed.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Proper Bearing Against the Many (Versions for Melee and Brawl)</span></span></span></b><br /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost: 5m; Type: Reflexive; Duration: Until Next Turn</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Exalt is a duelist, and as such is his style that he is unchallenged by their foes' cowardice. Until his next turn, he may reduce Onslaught penalties, and the bonuses of attack formations that attack them, reducing the penalties and bonuses by his Melee level. For instance, if a character with melee three is attacked by five enemies, he gets zero onslaugh penalty from the first five enemies, getting -1 from the fifth attacker.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Amoth's Blessing: The Exalt may renew this charm for four motes if he describes defensive stunts that destroy the constructions.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Beautiful Destruction (Melee or Brawl)</span></span></span></b><br /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost: 2 motes, Mins: Melee/Brawl 1, Essence 1</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Type: Supplemental</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Keywords: None</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration: Instant</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Pre-Reqs: None</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The user can use this saber to ignore the hardness of buildings for 1m. If the user stunts damage to an old building with this charm, double the dice bonus. Only buildings older than 100 years can be affected by this charm, but it can be used to create openings, ignore concealment on older constructions.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Battle-Formation Cry (Combina\u00e7\u00e3o de Charmes)</span></span></span></b><br /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost: 10m, 1w, Duration: Instant</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">In the chaotic mess of the battlefield, the Exalt may bring order to his brother in arms. The exalt may organize a group of people who are aligned with him in an ad-hoc battle group using this charm. The drill of the group depends on the training it has, from poor to elite. It can only be used once per scene. The Exalt may use this charm in the beggining of a combat, doubling the initiative of any battle groups he commands. If this charm is used to reorganize a dispersed battle group, it returns with one less size.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Amoth Blessing: By destroying an old building, the exalt may use this charm again. The group that is returned with this activation gains a major motivation and a specialty: sack and pillage.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#434343\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Social</span></span></b><br /><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Uncouth Barbarian Rebuke</span></span></span></b><br /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost: 2m; Mins: Presence 3, Essence 1</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Type: Supplemental</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Keywords: Amoth</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration: Instant</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Pre-reqs: TBD</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">If the Exalt is in numerical inferiority, he may call upon the proper rules of combat and compel his enemies to act in a civilized way. This charm supplements a presence roll to compel his enemies to follow regimented rules of combat (one on one, no assistence), working as if their enemies had a minor intimacy to 'proper combat', and removes the -3 penlty from multiple targets. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Amoth's Blessing: If the Exalt attacks a building he is near to show his dispossession, he gains double stunt bonuses. </span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Daring Swashbuckler's Smile</span></span></span></b><br /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost: 3m; Mins: Performance 3, Essence 1</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Type: Reflexive</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Keywords: Amoth, Stackable</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration: One Scene</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Pre-reqs: TBD</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The more he fights, the better he looks. The Exalt may use this Charm to raise his appearance by one each time he ends a turn without taking damage, or if he starts a turn in numerical inferiority. He may use this charm up to essence times.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Amoth's Blessing: If the Exalt destroys a building or irreplaceble historical object, he may use this charm one time this turn, this activation doesn't count to the limit, this may be used up to (highest combat ability) times.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1524-pcontop","name":"pcontop","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1524_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-14T19:24:55-07:00","id":931758,"title":"","content":"This is a very cool idea.<br /> <br /> One suggestion I'd have is that, since beauty is a huge part of this design, the stunted dice maximum should simply be (Appearance + Ability), instead of using the relevant attribute. Appearance represents not just the physical appearance of one's self but also the appearance of one's actions (hence why you can Command with it). Either that, or just make the excellency just based on Appearance and have the stunt add the ability.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12091-ignisdomini","name":"IgnisDomini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12091_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-14T19:53:11-07:00","id":931772,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the idea of beauty if more on the actions and style than on the practitioner. It's fighting as a cerimonial tool.<br /> <br /> I don't know if basing all caps on a single attribute is a good idea, design-wise, it would be even more unbalanced with Daring Swashbuckler's Smile doing double-duty as a dice-adder.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1524-pcontop","name":"pcontop","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1524_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}